    "created_at": "2023-09-04T11:31:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-09-04T11:31:37Z",
    "body": "> I want to add [popover=manual] and call showPopover only when \"necessary\", so I need a way to know whether a page has used popover and activated a top layer.\r\n\r\nWhy can't you just always use showPopover? You could feature detect it for browsers which don't support it yet like this:\r\n```javascript\r\nconst element = ...;\r\nif (HTMLElement.prototype.showPopover) {\r\n  element.setAttribute('popover', 'manual');\r\n  element.showPopover();\r\n} else {\r\n  element.style.position = 'fixed';\r\n  element.style.zIndex = '99999';\r\n}\r\n```",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
